        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "marine-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Marine Biology - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SUNLIT ZONE (0-200 m)            ← PRIMARY PRODUCTION ENGINE\n  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Phytoplankton: ~50% of Earth's O₂ production            │\n  │  Zooplankton, fish larvae, marine mammals, seabirds       │\n  │  Coral reefs: 0.1% of ocean floor, ~25% of species       │\n  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n               │ Biological Pump (sinking particles)\n               ▼\n  TWILIGHT ZONE (200-1000 m)        ← ACTIVE MIGRATION LAYER\n  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Diel vertical migrants: feed at surface at night         │\n  │  Lanternfishes, krill, squid, siphonophores               │\n  │  Largest daily animal migration on Earth (by biomass)     │\n  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n               │\n               ▼\n  MIDNIGHT ZONE (1000-4000 m)       ← PERMANENT DARKNESS\n  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  No light. Pressure: 100-400 atm                          │\n  │  Bioluminescence: dominant signaling modality             │\n  │  Marine snow (detritus) as primary food source            │\n  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n               │\n               ▼\n  ABYSSAL ZONE (4000-6000 m)        ← VAST DEEP PLAINS\n  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Covers ~60% of Earth's surface — least studied           │\n  │  Abyssal plains: soft sediment, polymetallic nodules      │\n  │  Pressure: 400-600 atm. Temperature: 0-3°C               │\n  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n               │\n               ▼\n  HADAL ZONE (>6000 m)              ← TRENCH ECOSYSTEMS\n  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  Ocean trenches: subduction zones. 37 total worldwide     │\n  │  Mariana Trench: 10,935 m (Challenger Deep)               │\n  │  Amphipods, holothurians, bacteria under extreme pressure  │\n  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
